{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-11y.2.1:000001:issue_created:sase-11y.2.1:90b6f3c08275ce2abc11698f1b5471afb6dc92f064dec665dfc1d296798598c0","timestamp":"2026-09-16T19:15:24Z","actor":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-11y.2","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"sase-11y.2.1","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"sase-11y.2.1","title":"sase-core service foundations","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":"sase-11y.2","owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-09-16T19:15:24Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-11y.2","updated_at":"2026-09-16T19:15:24Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"sase-core owns every piece of shared service-host behavior that later phases of the service-host epic (sase-11y) build on: the proc-wire `service` block with per-service retention, the `service.procs` config composer, the pure restart-decision function, the locked boot-scoped service state store, and the versioned service status snapshot. Each piece has PyO3 bindings and a thin typed Python facade, and the Procs query dialect gains the `service` and `svc:` fields.","design":"plan:202609/core_service_foundations.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","dependencies":[]}}}
